      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-206",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcsin x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(3{x}^{2})) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3{x}^{2})^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{4}}}\\cdot (6x) \\\\  & =\\frac{30x}{\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979604/example-206.json",
          "file_sha256": "149d038455976efdb9734693647a2811a3e88d9a7fe66e204e323e4a3b0b987d"
