      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-203",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arccos x) = -\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(5-8x)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5-8x)^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5-8x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(25-80x+64{x}^{2})}}\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{80x-24-64{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4(20x-6-16{x}^{2})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2\\sqrt{20x-6-16{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{20x-6-16{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979604/example-203.json",
