          "question": "e-202",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arctan x) = \\dfrac{1}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(-7x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(-7x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-7x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+49{x}^{2}}\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{1+49{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
